              "candidateEvaluations": [
                {
                  "id": "candidate-02",
                  "version": "agent.2",
                  "label": "Fuse elementwise multiply and last-dim reduction into one cuBLAS kernel",
                  "title": "Fuse elementwise multiply and last-dim reduction into one cuBLAS kernel",
                  "hypothesis": "At 32x256 the operator is launch-latency bound (~3us per kernel launch, measured from the 11.264us -> 8.192us delta when candidate-01 removed one launch). Rewriting the row-wise sum of products as a batched (rows,1,cols)@(rows,cols,1) matrix product collapses mul+sum into a single cuBLAS launch, so p50 should drop to roughly one launch plus fixed overhead, i.e. ~5us, instead of the current two launches at 8.192us.",
                  "change": "run(inputs) now returns torch.bmm(inputs['x'].unsqueeze(1), inputs['y'].unsqueeze(2)).view(-1). The unsqueezes and view(-1) are metadata-only (no device kernels), so exactly one kernel launch remains. torch.backends.cuda.matmul.allow_tf32 is set to False at import (guarded by try/except) so cuBLAS cannot silently select TF32 tensor-core kernels, which would break the atol/rtol=1e-5 comparison against the fp32-accumulating reference. get_inputs, get_test_cases, get_benchmark_inputs and reference are unchanged from the baseline, and shapes are preserved: (rows,1,1).view(-1) -> (rows,) matches reference(inputs) for every case (1x1, 32x256, 2x32, 3x17).",
