                        "title": "Eliminate redundant output clone and fold eps in-place",
                        "direction": "In run(inputs): replaced `value = inputs['x'] * torch.rsqrt((inputs['x'] * inputs['x']).mean(dim=-1, keepdim=True) + 1e-5); return value.clone()` with `x = inputs['x']; ms = torch.mean(x * x, dim=-1, keepdim=True); return x * torch.rsqrt(ms.add_(1e-5))`. Kernel count drops from 6 to 5; the full-size output allocation drops from 2 to 1. The in-place add is safe because `ms` is a freshly allocated tensor returned by torch.mean, never a view of the caller's input, so inputs are not mutated and repeated calls with the same inputs remain valid.",
